Emphasis on clear, structured frameworks such as GRI, SASB, or TCFD for standardized reporting. (2) Board Diversity: Issuers are required to maintain and disclose a board diversity policy addressing gender, skills, experience, and other aspects, alongside specific targets and progress updates. These amendments aim to align corporate governance practices in Singapore with international standards, fostering transparency, accountability, and investor confidence.', 'The Enhancements to Sustainability Reporting Regime and Board Diversity Disclosures, part of the SGX Mainboard Rules Amendments, introduce stricter reporting obligations for listed issuers in Singapore. These changes emphasize the importance of Environmental, Social, and Governance (ESG) factors and board diversity in corporate governance. The key amendments include: (1) Sustainability Reporting: Mandatory annual sustainability reports that include material ESG factors, climate-related disclosures (aligned with TCFD recommendations), policies, targets, and a board statement. Issuers must explain any exclusion of required reporting components and ensure internal or external assurance of sustainability reports.
Emphasis on clear, structured frameworks such as GRI, SASB, or TCFD for standardized reporting. (2) Board Diversity: Issuers are required to maintain and disclose a board diversity policy addressing gender, skills, experience, and other aspects, alongside specific targets and progress updates. These amendments aim to align corporate governance practices in Singapore with international standards, fostering transparency, accountability, and investor confidence.', 'The Enhancements to Sustainability Reporting Regime and Board Diversity Disclosures, part of the SGX Mainboard Rules Amendments, introduce stricter reporting obligations for listed issuers in Singapore. These changes emphasize the importance of Environmental, Social, and Governance (ESG) factors and board diversity in corporate governance. The key amendments include: (1) Sustainability Reporting: Mandatory annual sustainability reports that include material ESG factors, climate-related disclosures (aligned with TCFD recommendations), policies, targets, and a board statement. Issuers must explain any exclusion of required reporting components and ensure internal or external assurance of sustainability reports.
Emphasis on clear, structured frameworks such as GRI, SASB, or TCFD for standardized reporting. (2) Board Diversity: Issuers are required to maintain and disclose a board diversity policy addressing gender, skills, experience, and other aspects, alongside specific targets and progress updates. These amendments aim to align corporate governance practices in Singapore with international standards, fostering transparency, accountability, and investor confidence.', 'Singapore', 'climate', 'in_force', '2022-01-01'::date, 'Singapore', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/160_18', ARRAY['sdg13', 'mandatory', 'singapore', 'sdg5', 'sdg16', 'mandatory_regulations', 'sdg12', 'disclosure']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

The Act sets the carbon tax rate per tonne of CO2e and introduces a monitoring and reporting mechanism to ensure compliance. It also provides for the use of carbon credits for tax payment, subject to specific conditions. To maintain transparency and accountability, the law outlines penalties for non-compliance, inaccurate reporting, and other violations. Appeals mechanisms are also included, with provisions for review by an Appeal Panel or the High Court.', 'The Carbon Pricing Act, 2018, implemented in Singapore, establishes a comprehensive framework for carbon taxation and greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions reporting. The legislation applies to industrial facilities emitting GHGs at or above prescribed thresholds, requiring them to register as taxable or reportable facilities. Taxable facilities are subject to a carbon tax based on the amount of emissions, while both categories are mandated to submit annual emissions reports verified by accredited third-party auditors.

